006. C is the circumcenter of \Delta EBD [11] & E,D,C are collinear [04] ⇒  BE ⟂ BD [12]
007. AC = AB [00] & AF = AB [05] & AD = AB [02] ⇒  B,D,C,F are concyclic [13]
008. B,D,C,F are concyclic [13] ⇒  ∠BCD = ∠BFD [14]
009. ∠AFB = ∠FBA [07] & B,E,F are collinear [06] & ∠BAC = ∠BCD [09] & BD ⟂ AC [10] & BE ⟂ BD [12] & ∠BCD = ∠BFD [14] ⇒  ∠(DF-AC) = ∠FAC [15]
010. ∠(DF-AC) = ∠FAC [15] ⇒  DF ∥ AF [16]
011. DF ∥ AF [16] ⇒  A,D,F are collinear
